    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This part of the Procurement Journey is to help you develop commodity/service strategies.",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "A commodity/service strategy is always required for Route 3 procurement exercises.",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "If you are unable to estimate the value of a contract that contract will be explicitly made subject to the procurement rules.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The commodity/service strategy should be proportionate to the risk, value and strategic importance of the commodity/service to the Organisation. Consideration must also be given to Planning , Sustainable Procuremen t considerations and Risk Management .",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "A commodity/service strategy is different from a Procurement Strategy. The Procurement Strategy is a mandatory legislative requirement under The Procurement Reform (Scotland) Act 2014 for an Organisation which estimate the value of its regulated procurement will be equal to or greater than £5,000,000 (excluding VAT) in one year.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Quickfire Guide",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Sign Off Points",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "There are natural break points within the Procurement Journey that can be used as review points for sign off and approval to proceed to the next stage of the process.",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Suggested review and sign off points are:",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "At Project Initiation",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "After Initial Opportunity Assessment",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "For approval of Strategy including budget",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "For approval of Contract Notice , Selection Stage and/or ITT",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "At Contract Award stage",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "At Implementation stage",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Throughout the Procurement Journey, you will see reference to these sign off points at the relevant sections, as well as documents/templates for your use. Any review and agreement to the project plan should be in line with your organisation's governance arrangements.",
      "ordinal": 16,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00017",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The individual stations under Develop Commodity/Service Strategy provide guidance to assist you in completing the Develop Strategy template at the bottom of this page.",
      "ordinal": 17,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00018",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "You do not need to use all of the elements contained in this template for your strategy: use the areas which are relevant to your specific procurement exercise. To save this template in a version that you can edit yourself, click on the template hyperlink below, right mouse click over the \"Open File\" link and select the option \"Save Target As\".",
      "ordinal": 18,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00019",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Further information on Procurement Strategy requirements is available in Additional Resources .",
      "ordinal": 19,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00020",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
      "ordinal": 20,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00021",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "When developing your commodity/service strategy, you should access the contracts register for your organisation. This will assist in evaluating existing contract arrangements, including contract value.",
      "ordinal": 21,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00022",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Contracts Register module in Public Contracts Scotland (PCS) provides the facility for buying organisations to operate a register of all contracts they have in place. A public register of contracts meets the obligations of Section 35 of the Procurement Reform Act (Scotland) 2014.",
      "ordinal": 22,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00023",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "If you do not use PCS for producing a contract register, you still must produce a publicly available one.",
      "ordinal": 23,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00024",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
      "ordinal": 24,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00025",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "If using PCS-Tender , the Buyer should upload the appropriate slide s to the appropriate task within PCS-Tender.",
      "ordinal": 25,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00026",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Data Protection Regulation (DPR)",
      "ordinal": 26,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Data Protection Regulation (DPR)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00027",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Organisations should determine if data processing activities are relevant to your procurement exercise.",
      "ordinal": 27,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Data Protection Regulation (DPR)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00028",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Contracts that are currently subject to the Data Protection Act 1998 are also likely to be subject to DPR.",
      "ordinal": 28,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Data Protection Regulation (DPR)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00029",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Organisations must ensure:",
      "ordinal": 29,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Data Protection Regulation (DPR)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00030",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "current and future procurement exercises are compliant with DPR. This includes contracts that began before the legislation came into force",
      "ordinal": 30,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Data Protection Regulation (DPR)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00031",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "all relevant procurement documents make reference to the new legislation.",
      "ordinal": 31,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Data Protection Regulation (DPR)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00032",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "More detailed information on DPR can be found in Additional Resources .",
      "ordinal": 32,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Data Protection Regulation (DPR)"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00033",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Freedom of Information",
      "ordinal": 33,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Freedom of Information"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00034",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Please note that if you withhold the contract value from a contract award notice this information may still be requested from your organisation via the Freedom Of Information (Scotland) Act 2002 (FOISA) .",
      "ordinal": 34,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Freedom of Information"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00035",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The FOISA equivalent test is set much higher than the Contracts Register i.e. publication would have to, or be likely to:",
      "ordinal": 35,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Freedom of Information"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00036",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "cause substantial prejudice, and",
      "ordinal": 36,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Freedom of Information"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00037",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "the impact to public interest in withholding the information would have to outweigh the public interest in releasing it.",
      "ordinal": 37,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Freedom of Information"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00038",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Detailed contracts register user guidance can be found in PCS .",
      "ordinal": 38,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Freedom of Information"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00039",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Care and Support Services",
      "ordinal": 39,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Care and Support Services"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00040",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "For Care and Support Services procurements, Buyers must use Route 3 Develop Strategy stations and sub-stations to develop their service strategy and plan their approach to the procurement.",
      "ordinal": 40,
      "heading_path": [
        "Sign Off Points",
        "What If You Don't Use PCS to Publish Your Contract Register?",
        "What if You Use PCS-Tender?",
        "Care and Support Services"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00041",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Any documents you need are listed below",
      "ordinal": 41,
